  "query_preview": "..Today and Friday...We remain in a quiet weather pattern\ndominated by high pressure. Ridging will continue to build to our\nwest, with heights aloft peaking on Friday. Daytime highs will \nwarm to 10-15 degrees above normal for many, the exception is for\nvalleys east of the Mogollon Rim where low-level inversions will \nkeep temperatures closer to normal. Overall, expect pleasant \nweather each day with dry conditions and generally light winds.\n\nSaturday through Monday...By Saturday, ridging to our west starts to \nretreat as a series of shortwaves begins to brush past northern \nArizona. These disturbances will remain mostly dry for us, with \nthe primary impacts being periods of strong westerly winds and a \nslight cooling trend for those west of the Mogollon Rim. Breezy \nconditions are forecast for Saturday and Monday where gusts to \n25-35 mph are possible. Localized gusts near 40 mph will be \npossible north of the White Mountains.\n\nTuesday and onward...The ensemble consensus is for a stronger trough \nto move across northern Arizona towards the middle of next week. The \ncurrent forecast calls for precipitation chances to return beginning \nTuesday evening and continuing through Wednesday. There is \npotential for strong winds, rain, and high elevation snow with \nthis system, but confidence is low and there is plenty of room for\nthe details to change. Stay tuned to future forecasts for \nupdates!",
